This is the unit of fan-out: one codex invocation per agent slot, started in parallel within a wave, gated on the prior wave's L3 + L5 (where applicable) clear.

## What's deliberately NOT in this plan

- v1.4.1+ scope (signal policy registry, durable invalidation, scoring factor library refactor, source taxonomy migration, prompt fingerprinting v2, runtime evaluator pass, async projection scale-out, longitudinal threading consumer, recommendations layer).
- The 7 spec-needs-review tickets that are contract-only (DOS-302, DOS-303, DOS-304, DOS-305, DOS-307). Their decisions are already absorbed into the 22-issue spine. Tickets stay open as decision references but produce no code in v1.4.0.
- DOS-326 as a standalone ticket — folded into W4-A (DOS-5) per the issue body's own direction.

## Risk register

| Risk | Mitigation |
|------|-----------|
| W3-C and W3-D collide on `services/claims.rs` and migration numbering | One agent (W3-C) writes the schema + write path first, opens PR; W3-D rebases on top. Single PR train, two reviewers. |
| W2-A `with_transaction_async` HRTB design slips | Acceptance criteria already permits sync-within-async fallback. Don't block W3 on the HRTB nicety. |
| W3-G backfill < 95% coverage on legacy `source_asof` | The 95% bar is in the DoD. If real coverage lands at 90–94%, escalate to founder before relaxing — don't quietly ship at 90%. |

