## Reviewer matrix (L0 plan + L2 diff domain slot)

The third reviewer slot in L0 and L2 is a domain specialist keyed to the agent's risk profile. Slots stack: a single agent can pull multiple domain reviewers if it touches multiple risk dimensions.

| Agent profile | Domain reviewer |
|---|---|
| Substrate / schema (W1, W2, W3-A/B/C/D, W4-A) | architect-reviewer |
| New SQL write path or Tauri command (W3-C, W3-D, W3-E, W4-C) | security-auditor |
| Migration / projection / hot-path (W1-B, W3-C, W3-D, W4-A) | performance-engineer |
| User-facing surface (W5-A, W5-B, W6-D) | accessibility-tester |
| Test infrastructure (W4-B, W6-A, W6-B, W6-C) | qa-expert |

Worked example: **W3-C (DOS-7)** triggers architect-reviewer (substrate) + security-auditor (new write path) + performance-engineer (migration + projection hot path). All three review the plan and the diff.

## Test suites — S, P, E

Three dedicated suites run at specified gates. Each has an owner agent **separate from the implementing agent**. Suites feed into L3.

### Suite S — Security

| Gate | Owner | Coverage |
|---|---|---|
| End of W3 | penetration-tester + security-auditor | SQL injection on every new write site (`services/claims.rs`, `derived_state.rs`, `write_fence.rs`); cross-tenant exposure paths; PII/secrets in logs; immutability-allowlist bypass attempts |
| End of W4 | security-auditor | Auth/authz on `invoke_ability` Tauri command; MCP actor-filter discovery; schema-validation on input JSON; capability-handle leakage |
| End of W6 | full re-run + compliance-auditor | DOS-287 cross-entity bleed reproduction blocked; no PII in fixtures; secrets handling end-to-end |

**Pass rule:** zero unaddressed findings before next wave or release. Findings ranked Critical/High block the gate; Medium filed as v1.4.1 issues.

### Suite P — Performance

| Gate | Owner | Coverage | Budget |
|---|---|---|---|
| End of W1 | performance-engineer + criterion benches | Migration fence overhead (epoch bump, drain, reconcile); per-entity invalidation under Multi | **Baseline establishment** — numbers locked here |
| End of W3 | performance-engineer + `/benchmark` | 9-mechanism backfill on representative dataset; projection latency in-tx; SAVEPOINT cost; SQLite writer-lane behavior under sync projection | Backfill < N min on M-row dataset (set in W3-C plan); projection p99 < 50ms (provisional, ratified at W1) |
| End of W4 | performance-engineer | Trust compiler math at claim-volume; freshness fallback hot path | Trust score p99 < 5ms (provisional) |
| End of W5 | performance-engineer | Pilot abilities vs legacy capability latency | No regression vs legacy p50/p99 |

