.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:347:  corroborating_source_ref TEXT,
.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:363:- The "three tombstone mechanisms already exist" finding means the migration story is larger than v1.4.0 alone. Flag for [DOS-7](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-7) design review: decide whether v1.4.0 ships the `intelligence_claims` table + schema + service functions but keeps existing tombstone tables authoritative, with full migration to v1.4.1.
.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:376:- `propose_claim` and `commit_claim` service functions with gate logic implemented but config set to `immediate` for all classes.
.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:377:- **Consolidation migrations active** (updated 2026-04-20 per plan-eng-review AskUserQuestion #1): `suppression_tombstones`, `DismissedItem` in-blob entries, and `account_stakeholder_roles.dismissed_at` values all backfilled into `intelligence_claims` as `tombstoned` rows. Reads switch to `intelligence_claims` for tombstone queries. Old tables kept read-only for parity testing.
