.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:70:`provenance_schema_version` is the schema version of this ADR's envelope structure. A consumer seeing a higher version must parse forward-compatibly — unknown fields are ignored; known fields retain their meaning. The initial version is `1`. Any breaking change requires a new version and a migration path.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:72:`ability_schema_version` is the ability's I/O schema version per [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §8 — a different concept, retained here for completeness so a consumer reading provenance knows exactly which ability contract produced the output.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:83:    pub provider_config_hash: Hash,                  // Hash of provider settings at invocation time
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:95:1. **Staleness detection.** A consumer renders "as of 14:23 UTC, freshest Glean sync 3 hours ago."
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:103:Trust is a structured record, not a collapsed nested enum. It encodes the weakest trust encountered, the mixing history, and whether the output is safe to authorize mutation on without a trust signal per [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §10.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:107:    /// The effective trust of this output for mutation-authorization purposes.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:110:    /// Contributions to the trust computation. Lists every ancestor whose
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:111:    /// output mixed into this one, annotated with why its trust class applies.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:121:    /// Safe to use for mutation authorization without a trust signal.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:126:    Untrusted,
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:143:    ComposedUntrustedChild,                // Child ability returned Untrusted
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:151:1. If `prompt_fingerprint.is_some()`, this ability invoked the LLM → `Untrusted`.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:152:2. If any `contributions[i]` has `reason == ComposedUntrustedChild` or `DirectlyFromLLMSynthesis` or `StoredSynthesis` or `UnboundedFreeText`, the output is `Untrusted`.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:156:**This closes the laundering hole.** A Read ability that returns stored AI output (e.g., a cached `entity_assessment.summary` from Glean) is `Untrusted` because the stored field itself carries a synthesis marker. The `contains_stored_synthesis` flag and `TrustReason::StoredSynthesis` contribution make the reasoning explicit.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:158:**`effective` is computed by the provenance builder, not the author.** The author cannot set it; the registry rejects manually-constructed `Provenance` with mismatched `effective` and `contributions`.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:162:Source attribution references the authoritative `DataSource` taxonomy in [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md). This ADR specifies the shape; that ADR specifies the enum values and lifecycle behavior.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:165:pub struct SourceAttribution {
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:166:    pub data_source: DataSource,                 // Defined by ADR-0107
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:169:    pub source_asof: Option<DateTime<Utc>>,      // When the source itself was authored (if known)
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:193:**`evidence_weight` is a contribution weight, not a reliability score.** It is author-supplied (by the ability's planner or synthesizer) and indicates how much this particular source mattered for this specific output. It is not a stored per-source reliability — those are defined by [ADR-0080](0080-signal-intelligence-architecture.md) and consumed separately. We deliberately do not duplicate ADR-0080's reliability into every provenance envelope.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:195:**`scoring_class` is derived from the `DataSource` per [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md).** It is informational, so consumers can filter context-only sources from scoring analysis.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:241:5. `FieldPath` uses JSON-Pointer syntax with a stability caveat: array-index paths (`/topics/0`) are tolerated for render-time display but are not stable across re-runs. Stable identifiers (`/topics/[id=abc123]/title`) SHOULD be used when the output structure contains stable IDs.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:245:When ability A invokes ability B, A's provenance includes B's as a nested `child`:
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:260:2. `trust.effective` merges bottom-up per the rules in §3.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:261:3. `prompt_fingerprint` does not merge — each ability has its own or none.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:263:5. Deduplication across `children[i].sources[]` is render-time, not construction-time.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:270:Contributors produce provenance via a builder that enforces the rules in §3 and §5:
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:282:        DataSource::Google,
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:289:    let account_child_idx = prov.compose(&account_ctx.provenance);
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:291:    // LLM synthesis — builder enforces that this triggers Untrusted trust
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:293:    prov.prompt_fingerprint(completion.fingerprint);  // Shape per ADR-0106
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:299:    ], Confidence::provider_reported(completion.confidence));
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:308:- Computes `trust.effective` from sources and composition.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:309:- Rejects manual overrides to computed fields (`trust.effective`, `contains_stored_synthesis`).
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:310:- Wraps the domain output in `AbilityOutput<T>` with the built provenance.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:317:1. **Maintenance audit table.** [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §8 `MaintenanceAuditRecord` adds a `provenance: Provenance` field. Source revocation triggers a masking pass: a `Provenance` whose sources reference a revoked `DataSource` is replaced with a `ProvenanceMasked` marker per [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md). **Interaction with [ADR-0094](0094-audit-log-and-enterprise-observability.md):** ADR-0094's append-only JSONL security audit remains unchanged. The `maintenance_audit` SQLite table is a separate operational log for runtime diagnostics. Provenance content in the operational log is subject to masking; the JSONL security log is unchanged.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:319:2. **Outbox table.** [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §2 outbox entries add a `provenance: Provenance` field. Outbox provenance captures the ability's full output-time provenance, including the invocation that generated the pending external mutation.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:321:3. **Planned mutations.** [ADR-0104](0104-execution-mode-and-mode-aware-services.md) §3 `PlannedMutation` adds a `provenance_ref: InvocationId` field pointing into the ability's provenance envelope. Plans do not carry a full duplicated provenance; they reference the envelope by invocation ID and field path, preventing storage duplication.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:325:**Storage format.** Provenance is stored as JSON in a single column per containing record. Indexes on `invocation_id`, `ability_name`, `produced_at`, and `data_source` (via a normalized xref table) support the queries [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §8 requires. A full JSON-column approach is feasible at the six-user scale; if scale changes, a normalized `provenance` / `provenance_sources` split can be introduced without changing the envelope contract.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:329:A typical Read ability produces ~500B–5KB of provenance. Transform abilities with field attributions can reach ~50KB. Deeply composed Maintenance invocations with >8 composition levels or >50 sources can exceed 500KB, which is excessive for per-invocation storage.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:331:**Soft budget.** Abilities SHOULD keep provenance under 100KB. The registry warns at build time when provenance exceeds the soft budget.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:333:**Hard truncation.** When a provenance envelope exceeds 1MB at finalize time, composition subtrees are collapsed from deepest first into a `ProvenanceWarning::DepthElided` summary carrying aggregate source counts and trust classification. Truncation is a finalize-time concern; the full tree never leaves the ability in its raw form above the hard limit.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:340:2. **Trust boundary is enforceable and closes the laundering hole.** [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §10 rejects mutations authorized by `Untrusted` output at the registry layer, and `contains_stored_synthesis` catches the case where stored AI output is surfaced by a Read ability.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:342:4. **Composition is explicit.** Nested provenance makes composition visible in output, not hidden in call stacks, with a stable `composition_id` avoiding positional brittleness.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:343:5. **Source revocation can cascade correctly.** Provenance references `DataSource` via [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md), and lifecycle behavior (purge vs. flag) is governed by that ADR. Masking shape is governed by [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md).
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:344:6. **Storage integration is explicit.** Maintenance audit, outbox, and plans each know exactly how they carry or reference provenance. Plans use references to avoid duplication.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:356:2. **Trust miscomputation.** The builder's trust computation misses a contribution. Mitigation: `contributions[]` is auditable — a failing case is a diagnosable bug with an explicit contribution list, not a silent `Untrusted`/`Trusted` flip.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:357:3. **Storage volume growth.** Provenance retained indefinitely alongside outputs accumulates. Mitigation: same retention as output; no separate provenance retention policy.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:360:6. **Forward-compatibility regressions.** A consumer written against `provenance_schema_version = 1` breaks when version `2` adds a required variant. Mitigation: breaking changes require a new `provenance_schema_version` and a deprecation window for consumers.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:364:- [ADR-0102: Abilities as the Runtime Contract](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) — Defines `AbilityOutput<T>` wrapper; §9 Rule 5 requires provenance; §10 consumes `TrustAssessment`; §11.3 requires composition merge.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:365:- [ADR-0103: Maintenance Ability Safety Constraints](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) — §8 maintenance audit records add a `provenance: Provenance` field per §8 of this ADR.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:366:- [ADR-0104: ExecutionMode and Mode-Aware Services](0104-execution-mode-and-mode-aware-services.md) — `mode` and clock injection for `produced_at`; `PlannedMutation` adds a `provenance_ref` field.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:367:- [ADR-0094: Audit Log and Enterprise Observability](0094-audit-log-and-enterprise-observability.md) — Coexistence: ADR-0094's append-only JSONL security audit is unchanged; this ADR's provenance lives in operational `maintenance_audit` SQLite table with masking.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:369:- **[ADR-0106: Prompt Fingerprinting and Provider Interface Extension](0106-prompt-fingerprinting-and-provider-interface.md)** — Specifies `PromptFingerprint` shape, canonicalization, and amendments to [ADR-0091](0091-intelligence-provider-abstraction.md).
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:370:- **[ADR-0107: Source Taxonomy Alignment](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md)** — Authoritative `DataSource` enum, `SourceIdentifier` extensibility, and lifecycle behavior per source class.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:371:- **[ADR-0108: Provenance Rendering and Privacy](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md)** — Per-surface rendering rules, actor-filtered display, `ProvenanceMasked` shape, sanitization of `explanation` text, and P2 publication safety.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:372:- **ADR-0109 (forthcoming): Temporal Primitives in the Entity Graph** — Defines trajectory types referenced from provenance when an ability consumes trajectory inputs.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:373:- **ADR-0110 (forthcoming): Evaluation Harness for Abilities** — Uses `prompt_fingerprint` and `field_attributions` for regression detection.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:374:- **ADR-0111 (forthcoming): Surface-Independent Ability Invocation** — References the rendering rules in [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md).
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:375:- **ADR-0112 (forthcoming): Migration Strategy — Parallel Run and Cutover** — Covers migration of existing stored AI content to carry `synthesis_marker` so the trust model's `contains_stored_synthesis` check works retroactively.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:379:## Amendment — 2026-04-24 — `source_asof` population semantics + `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:383:The 2026-04-24 Claim Anatomy Review (`.docs/plans/claim-anatomy-review-2026-04-24.md` §10) identified that `source_asof: Option<DateTime<Utc>>` exists in §4 above as optional metadata but no code path actually populates it. Today's storage path stamps `observed_at = now` (`glean_provider.rs:1182`) regardless of when the underlying source was authored. The Glean/PTY prompts ask for `sourcedAt` per item (`dimension_prompts.rs:608`) but the returned timestamp lives in a JSON blob and is never lifted into the first-class column.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:385:**Effective behavior today:** every claim freshly synthesized from a 6-month-old Salesforce note looks fresh. Trust Compiler's `freshness_weight` factor (DOS-10) will be calibrated against ingestion time, not evidence time. Stale evidence appears as fresh claims — load-bearing bug present today, that worsens when Trust Compiler ships unless fixed.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:391:`source_asof` is amended from "optional metadata" to **must-be-populated-when-knowable**, with an explicit population chain:
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:394:populate(source_asof) = pick first available:
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:401:If all four fail, `source_asof = None` AND the Provenance envelope emits a new warning variant:
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:420:Surfaces (per ADR-0108) render `SourceTimestampUnknown` so the system can see when freshness is being approximated rather than measured.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:424:The freshness factor uses an explicit fallback chain — **conservative on unknown**:
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:427:freshness_input_age = match (source_asof, observed_at):
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:437:The builder lifts `itemSource.sourcedAt` (when present in LLM output) and Glean document timestamps into `source_asof` automatically. Authors do not manually populate the field. The builder emits `SourceTimestampUnknown` when the population chain falls to step 4.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:443:| DOS-211 (Provenance Builder, spine) | Builder lifts `sourcedAt` from `itemSource` JSON or Glean document metadata into `source_asof`. Emits `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning on full fallback. |
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:444:| DOS-5 (Trust Compiler, spine) | `freshness_weight` factor uses the fallback chain in §B above. Conservative on unknown. |
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:446:| DOS-218 / DOS-219 (pilot abilities, spine) | Acceptance criteria include: produces ≥1 claim with `source_asof` populated and ≥1 claim with `SourceTimestampUnknown` warning, demonstrating the chain works both ways. |
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:447:| `glean_provider.rs:1182` write path | Lift Glean document timestamps into `source_asof` before writing SignalEvent / claim row. Don't stamp `observed_at = now` as the only timestamp. |
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:452:The earlier draft of this amendment said "Backfill of historical claims is a non-goal; `source_asof` stays NULL on pre-amendment rows." **That was wrong.** Adversarial review surfaced that the existing `ItemSource.sourced_at` field in stored `intelligence.json` blobs IS the evidence-time timestamp, and is consumed today by suppression (`is_suppressed`) and timeliness logic (`services/accounts.rs:1253-1274`). Treating migrated claims as unknown-timestamp would apply `STALENESS_PADDING` to data whose timestamp is actually knowable — that's a regression dressed as conservatism.
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:457:backfill source_asof for each migrated claim:
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:459:     → source_asof = parsed timestamp
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:461:     → source_asof = None AND emit ProvenanceWarning::SourceTimestampUnknown { fallback: ObservedAt }
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:472:The migration applies these bounds to every parsed `source_asof`:
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:482:    → freshness factor treats as None (unknown) rather than honoring the implausible value
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:483:  - timestamp > now + 30 days (near-future; legitimate for renewal dates but suspicious for source_asof)
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:485:    → freshness factor treats as observed_at instead
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:489:  - quarantined claims are queryable via `intelligence_claims WHERE provenance_warnings @> 'SourceTimestampImplausible'`
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:498:- Auto-classifier for inferring `source_asof` from claim_text content (v1.5.x+).
.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:499:- Backfill of `source_asof` from sources OTHER than existing `ItemSource.sourced_at` (e.g., re-fetching Glean documents to recover their timestamps for old claims). This is post-spine cleanup if needed.

