     1	//! DOS-287: Cross-entity contamination validator.
     2	//!
     3	//! Second-line defense against Glean/PTY enrichment writing content about a
     4	//! different customer into the target account's intelligence record. Runs
     5	//! immediately before persistence: if the generated narrative mentions
     6	//! another account's domain, WP-VIP host, or company name (and the target's
     7	//! own name is not also present), the write is rejected and a signal is
     8	//! emitted so the frontend can toast.
     9	//!
    10	//! Heuristics (evaluated in order; first hit wins per unique token):
    11	//!   1. Foreign domain match — any `account_domains.domain` for a non-target
    12	//!      non-archived account, whole-word.
    13	//!   2. Foreign vip-*.com host — matches `vip[0-9]*-[a-z]+\.com` and
    14	//!      `vip[0-9]+\.[a-z]+\.com`. If the host is not in the target's known
    15	//!      domains, it's foreign.
    16	//!   3. Foreign company name — any `accounts.name` for a non-target
    17	//!      non-archived account, normalized, whole-word, ≥4 chars, excluding
    18	//!      `STOPLIST` terms. Suppressed when the target's own name also appears
    19	//!      in the text (legitimate comparison).
    20	//!
    21	//! Matching is case-insensitive; bounded by non-alphanumeric characters.
    22	//!
    23	//! TODO(DOS-282): Regression fixtures for vip2-msd.com / Merck cross-bleed
    24	//! should live with that ticket.
    25	
    26	use crate::db::ActionDb;
